WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.433 --> 00:00:08.373
The first film drew one wheel, gold after meiosis and teal after fusion.

2
00:00:09.853 --> 00:00:12.453
Now, at the top of a pine there is no water film.

3
00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.353
So how does a sperm reach an egg?

4
00:00:16.333 --> 00:00:19.213
The pine tree is the sporophyte, so it is teal.

5
00:00:20.473 --> 00:00:24.373
Its cones make two kinds of spores, so the gold arc splits in two.

6
00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:28.957
In small pollen cones, meiosis makes microspores.

7
00:00:30.317 --> 00:00:31.897
Each one becomes a pollen grain.

8
00:00:33.137 --> 00:00:34.817
A pollen grain is not a sperm.

9
00:00:36.057 --> 00:00:38.257
It is a male gametophyte of a few cells.

10
00:00:39.317 --> 00:00:43.897
In larger seed cones, meiosis inside an ovule gives four megaspores.

11
00:00:45.297 --> 00:00:46.317
Only one survives.

12
00:00:47.637 --> 00:00:50.737
It grows into the female gametophyte, which forms eggs.

13
00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:54.017
Wind carries pollen to the ovule.

14
00:00:55.217 --> 00:00:59.677
A pollen tube grows and delivers sperm to the egg, with no outside water.

15
00:01:00.997 --> 00:01:03.197
Both gametophytes are still here, just shrunk.

16
00:01:04.417 --> 00:01:06.897
The female one stays inside the ovule.

17
00:01:07.957 --> 00:01:09.637
The male one travels as pollen.

18
00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:13.167
The egg is fertilized, and a seed forms.

19
00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:17.727
The seed's food store grew from that surviving megaspore.

20
00:01:19.207 --> 00:01:20.207
Gold or teal?

21
00:01:26.433 --> 00:01:32.113
Gold. The food store is the female gametophyte, so it is haploid.

22
00:01:33.353 --> 00:01:35.693
The seed coat comes from the parent tree, teal.

23
00:01:36.833 --> 00:01:39.233
The embryo is the new sporophyte, teal too.

24
00:01:40.453 --> 00:01:42.193
One seed holds three generations.

25
00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:47.147
Flowering plants shrink the female gametophyte even further.

26
00:01:48.447 --> 00:01:51.307
Here too, the pollen grain is the male gametophyte.

27
00:01:52.327 --> 00:01:57.147
In Arabidopsis, the female one is the embryo sac, inside the ovule.

28
00:01:58.527 --> 00:02:01.467
Meiosis gives four megaspores, and three degenerate.

29
00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:06.740
The survivor's nucleus divides three times, without making new cells.

30
00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:14.200
Then walls form. Two cells matter here: the egg, and a large central cell holding

31
00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.200
two nuclei.

32
00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:19.190
Those two are the polar nuclei, and both are gold.

33
00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:23.390
In Arabidopsis they fuse before fertilization.

34
00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.490
Fusion adds, so the central cell is now 2n.

35
00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:30.490
A pollen tube brings two sperm.

36
00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:34.530
One fuses with the egg, giving a teal zygote.

37
00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:37.710
The other fuses with the central cell.

38
00:02:39.433 --> 00:02:40.873
Fusion adds again.

39
00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:46.033
The result is endosperm, a food tissue, and it carries three sets.

40
00:02:47.313 --> 00:02:51.253
That holds in Arabidopsis and most flowering plants, but not all.

41
00:02:52.267 --> 00:02:54.647
Every label came from the same two gates.

42
00:02:56.007 --> 00:02:58.627
Meiosis halves the sets, and fusion adds them.

43
00:03:00.187 --> 00:03:05.127
Size and place changed, but meiosis still starts each gametophyte, and fertilization

44
00:03:05.127 --> 00:03:09.347
each sporophyte. Extra fusions add the endosperm.

45
00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:13.747
The female gametophyte now stays inside the ovule.
